{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Upon children and upon children's children, etc.</b> Here He added ״בְּנֵי בָנִים,״ something He did not mention either in the first Decalogue or in the second, because with idolatry the measure is always thus — to the fourth generation, and it begins counting from the father: the father is first, the son is second, and afterward the third generation, and afterward the fourth. But in the matter of the Golden Calf, all the worshippers had already received their punishment and the iniquity was forgiven for that generation, but not for future generations. And in order to fulfill the accounting for four generations, it was necessary to count from the son and add one generation and count: children, and children's children — the third, and the fourth. And this is what it says: ״וּבְיוֹם פָּקְדִי״ (Exodus 32:34) — that is, when the time of the accounting shall come, then ״וּפָקַדְתִּי עֲלֵיהֶם״ — that time of accounting stated in the Ten Commandments. And in my opinion, because the iniquity of idolatry is more severe than all the other iniquities, a single generation cannot bear the greatness of the punishment fitting to come upon this iniquity; therefore it is divided among four generations to lighten and not to make harsher. And there are those who say the opposite of this, for thus it says: ״וַיְמַהֵר מֹשֶׁה וַיִּקֹּד אַרְצָה״ (Exodus 34:8) — Moses saw that the Holy One, blessed be He, was calling the generations from the beginning and proceeding and counting and adding one generation, and he was afraid lest He continue to add and strike through several generations; therefore Moses hurried and bowed to the ground and said, 'Enough for You!'"], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The final quotation 'דַּיֶּךָּ' (enough for You) alludes to the Midrashic tradition of Moses crying out 'די' to halt the expansion of punishment; rendered as direct speech following the idiom."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:25:15.725350322Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}